  I read the test bodies rather than trusting the names
  (/home/darrell/bin/ai/budget2/internal/handlers/whatif/handlers_sweep_test.go:492-759):
   - The three tie tests feed rows in AMOUNT-DESCENDING order, so a pass cannot be an artifact of
     iteration order; each asserts the smaller-amount row wins AND the larger one does not.
   - SurvivesBeatsAnyDepletion pits DepletionMonth=5000 (not surviving) against Survives=true with
     EndingBalanceReal=1 and asserts the survivor wins — the rule, not a coincidence.
   - CombinedMarker asserts both flags true on one row and neither on the other.
   - TestConversionSweepApply_ThroughRealRouter is a genuine end-to-end flow:
       r := chi.NewRouter(); RegisterRoutes(r); ts := httptest.NewServer(r)
       http.PostForm(ts.URL+"/whatif/roth-conversion", {apply_source=conversion-sweep,
                     annual_amount=100000, enabled=on, start_year=3, end_year=12})
